==English==
[[Image:Athabasca.Moulin.jpg|thumb|Meltwater flowing into a '''moulin''']]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|moulin|}}, from {{der|en|LL.|molinum||mill}}. {{doublet|en|moline|mill}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmuːlæn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|geology}} A cylindrical, vertical [[shaft]] that extends through a [[glacier]] and is carved by [[meltwater]] from the glacier’s surface.

